3. Prohibition of plastic covers for books.—(1) No seller shall sell, offer for sale or otherwise distribute any book within the Territory that is encased, wrapped, or covered in a plastic cover which is meant only for carrying purposes.
(2) The prohibition of sub-section (1) shall not apply to-
(a) packaged in materials certified as biodegradable or compostable in accordance with prescribed environmental standards;

(b) covered with reusable, non-plastic materials intended for long-term personal or institutional use;

(c) enclosed in archival, preservation or protective packaging for rare, antique or precious items for collectible purposes, as may be prescribed;

(d) designed with plastic components that form an integral and necessary part of their construction, such as laminated hardback covers;

(e) part of a special collection, library, or archive requiring plastic covering for preservation, in accordance with guidelines issued by the competent authority; or

(f) Books themselves are made of such material or such material is part of the books in any manner whatsoever.

5. Power to make rules.—(1) The Federal Government may, by notification in the official Gazette, make rules for carrying out the purposes of this Act.—
(2) Without prejudice to the generality of the foregoing power, such rules may provide for,—
(a) the manner in which exemptions under sub-section (2) of section 3 may be granted;
(b) the procedure for the enforcement of this Act and the imposition of penalties;

(c) the appointment of enforcement officers and their powers and duties; and
(d) any other matter necessary for the implementation of this Act.
